BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:October Mushroom Curiosity Walk
DTSTART:20261017T093000
DTEND:20261017T113000
DTSTAMP:20261017T141651Z
UID:8cf8c8b55469ce636af88bcf4c8c65@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join renowned mushroom photographer\, accomplished author\, co
 mmunity science advocate\, and mycology educator\, Meg Madden\, on a mushr
 oom curiosity walk to learn more about the lives of these fascinating orga
 nisms. As we explore the woods we'll talk about the mushrooms we find alon
 g the way including what they are and how to identify them. From cycling n
 utrients to connecting trees\, we will talk about the essential roles that
  fungi play within their natural communities. Meg will also discuss the im
 portance of community science\, how you can contribute to Vermont's growin
 g database of fungi species on iNaturalist\, and share tips and tricks for
  taking scientific grade mushroom photos. Wear comfortable walking shoes\,
  weather-appropriate clothing\, and bring your questions and curiosity! A 
 smartphone equipped with the iNaturalist app is a plus\, but not required.
 \n\nSources: Vermont Public
LOCATION:Green Mountain Audubon Center — Sugarhouse Parking Area\, 368 M
 ain Road
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/october-mu
 shroom-curiosity-walk-15-10-2026-12-41-16
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Opening Events for The Grief Center of Vermont
DTSTART:20261017T120000
DTEND:20261017T173000
DTSTAMP:20261017T141651Z
UID:831afaa561c1b2ca7b075cc6555645@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Please come check out our new community space\, The Grief Cent
 er of Vermont\, opening in Essex Junction on October 17! The Grief Center 
 is a place for people to find community\, connection\, creativity\, or sup
 port through all forms of grief\, loss\, and change. You could be contempl
 ating divorce or the end of a major relationship\, mourning the death of a
  loved one\, experiencing ecological grief\, carrying the weight of person
 al or professional caregiving\, or facing life after retirement. All exper
 iences are welcome here. You do not have to have the right words\, have it
  more together\, or be falling apart more to benefit from community and co
 nnection. We have support circles\, long and short-term retreats\, communi
 ty events\, educational workshops\, and 1:1 doula services to suit everyon
 e. 137 Iroquois Avenue Essex Junction \, Vermont 05452 8024042144 jess@gri
 efcenterofvermont.com https://www.griefcenterofvermont.com Submit An Event
