BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Tony Vacca's Fusion Nomads w/ Massamba Diop
DTSTART:20261017T180000
DTEND:20261017T200000
DTSTAMP:20261017T141651Z
UID:39ec305500e4759b1563cab72bf100@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Tony Vacca’s Fusion Nomads brings together musicians whose i
 ndividual journeys through jazz\, global traditions\, and improvisation cr
 eate a richly textured\, boundary-crossing sound. Led by innovative percus
 sionist and balafon player Tony Vacca\, the ensemble features Jo Sallins o
 n electric bass and percussion\, Charles Langford on saxophone\, and John 
 Sheldon on harp-guitar. Special guest Massamba Diop—master of the Senega
 lese tama\, or talking drum\, and longtime member of Baaba Maal’s world-
 renowned band—joins the group for this dynamic concert. Diop’s recent 
 work includes featured appearances on the soundtracks for Black Panther an
 d Black Panther: Wakanda Forever. Drawing on Vacca’s decades of work in 
 jazz and world music\, including extensive study and performance in West A
 frica\, Fusion Nomads weaves tradition and innovation into music that move
 s freely across borders\, rhythms\, and styles. Next Stage Arts\n\nSources
 : Vermont Public
LOCATION:Vermont Public is independent\, community-supported media\, servi
 ng Vermont with trusted\, relevant and essential information. We share sto
 ries that bring people together\, from every corner of our region.\, © 20
 26 Vermont Public | 365 Troy Ave. Colchester\, VT 05446
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/tony-vacca
 s-fusion-nomads-w-massamba-diop-18-09-2026-20-19-25
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Walk to Prevent Suicide in Burlington on October 17
DTSTART:20261017T090000
DTEND:20261017T120000
DTSTAMP:20261017T141651Z
UID:bf5530a86d42e78dc45d55c7f94576@vermont-events
DESCRIPTION:Join the American Foundation for Suicide Prevention Vermont Ch
 apter for the Burlington Out of the Darkness Walk on Saturday\, October 17
 \, 2026\, at Veterans Memorial Park in South Burlington. Check-in begins a
 t 9:00 a.m.\; the program starts at 10:00 a.m. Walk with suicide loss surv
 ivors\, people with lived experience\, families\, friends\, advocates\, an
 d community partners to honor loved ones\, reduce stigma\, and support sui
 cide prevention. Registration is free\, and the non-competitive walk will 
 be 1–3 miles. Participants can register\, form a team\, invite others\, 
 volunteer\, or sponsor the event. Funds raised support AFSP research\, adv
 ocacy\, survivor support\, and education across Vermont. To register\, don
 ate\, volunteer\, or learn more\, visit afspwalks.donordrive.com/Burlingto
 n. For sponsorship or volunteer questions\, contact Kathleen Weinheimer at
  kweinheimer.afsp@gmail.com or (802) 238-8085. The American Foundation for
  Suicide Prevention saves lives and brings hope to those affected by suici
 de through research\, education\, advocacy\, and survivor support. Learn m
 ore about the Vermont Chapter at afsp.org/vermont. If you or someone you k
 now is in crisis\, call or text 988 to reach the Suicide & Crisis Lifeline
 \, or chat at 988lifeline.org. In an emergency\, call 911.\n\nSources: Ver
 mont Public
LOCATION:Veterans Memorial Park\, 1000 Dorset Street
URL:https://www.vermontpublic.org/vermont-events-calendar/event/walk-to-pr
 event-suicide-in-burlington-on-october-17-30-09-2026-14-28-09
END:VEVENT
